WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:33.250
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:33.520 --> 01:36.080
As long as you are diagnosed with the disease specified in the contract

3
01:36.080 --> 01:38.080
or reach the condition specified in the contract,

4
01:38.080 --> 01:39.240
we can directly pay out

5
01:39.240 --> 01:39.680
up to hundreds of thousands in insurance money.

6
01:39.680 --> 01:40.800
Isn't that Lawyer Xiao?

7
01:40.800 --> 01:42.400
They pay out just like that? Yes.

8
01:42.400 --> 01:44.640
Is that her boyfriend next to her?

9
01:46.200 --> 01:47.960
Who could stand her temper?

10
01:48.800 --> 01:50.200
What boyfriend?

11
01:50.680 --> 01:51.680
That's a mascot.

12
01:51.680 --> 01:52.240
A mascot?

13
01:52.240 --> 01:53.800
The contents are all in here.

14
01:53.800 --> 01:54.840
This is the contract?

15
01:54.840 --> 01:55.120
Yes.

16
01:55.120 --> 01:56.039
It's so thick.

17
01:56.039 --> 01:57.570
I thought it was a magazine.

18
02:07.920 --> 02:10.039
What a coincidence, Lawyer Xiao.

19
02:10.039 --> 02:11.360
Such a coincidence.

20
02:13.240 --> 02:14.500
Critically ill child.

21
02:15.240 --> 02:17.640
Haven't seen you for a few days and you already have a child.

22
02:17.640 --> 02:18.570
Born yesterday.

23
02:18.760 --> 02:20.220
You recovered quite fast.

24
02:20.360 --> 02:21.240
Jealous?

25
02:22.000 --> 02:23.000
Excuse me, you two.

26
02:23.000 --> 02:24.960
I have other clients. I'll be leaving first.

27
02:24.960 --> 02:26.960
No problem. Go ahead with your work.

28
02:29.840 --> 02:31.079
Is she explaining it well?

29
02:31.079 --> 02:32.000
If there's anything you don't understand,

30
02:32.000 --> 02:33.840
I'll ask Mr. Wei to explain it to you personally.

31
02:33.840 --> 02:35.280
I don't understand you.

32
02:35.560 --> 02:37.400
Why do you always ruin my plans?

33
02:37.600 --> 02:40.800
Well, you can't come here and always ruin my plans either.

34
02:42.520 --> 02:43.320
Is it a boy or a girl?

35
02:43.320 --> 02:44.160
Give it a rest.

36
02:44.160 --> 02:46.890
No, if a girl looks like her father, she's ruined.

37
02:48.240 --> 02:50.160
Do you believe that after they take off their suits,

38
02:50.160 --> 02:52.560
there will be huge sweat stains right here?

39
02:53.160 --> 02:56.160
I believe it. I used to dress like that,

40
02:56.360 --> 02:57.560
sweating profusely.

41
02:59.160 --> 03:01.020
Why is there no sound in the video?

42
03:01.160 --> 03:02.090
Unfortunately,

43
03:02.280 --> 03:04.720
the camera in this reception room that day

44
03:05.080 --> 03:07.610
had a malfunction in its recording function.

45
03:08.160 --> 03:08.880
Lawyer Li.

46
03:09.400 --> 03:10.720
But this makes it impossible to confirm

47
03:10.720 --> 03:14.250
whether the salesperson fully fulfilled their duty to inform.

48
03:18.000 --> 03:19.400
Wait a moment, everyone.

49
03:55.720 --> 03:57.650
Sorry, everyone. Let's continue.

50
04:07.560 --> 04:08.480
What are you doing?

51
04:08.480 --> 04:10.610
What are you doing? What are you doing?

52
04:11.520 --> 04:12.440
I was just trying to hear

53
04:12.440 --> 04:15.000
what they were plotting with the insurance company.

54
04:15.000 --> 04:15.920
Did you hear anything?

55
04:15.920 --> 04:17.440
No. The glass is too thick.

56
04:18.399 --> 04:19.480
Isn't that embarrassing?

57
04:19.480 --> 04:21.160
This is an infringement of my portrait rights,

58
04:21.160 --> 04:21.920
you know?

59
04:21.920 --> 04:23.160
I could sue him for this.

60
04:23.160 --> 04:24.320
Let's go. I'll take you to sue him.

61
04:24.320 --> 04:25.080
Okay, okay.

62
04:25.080 --> 04:26.040
Let's get down to business.

63
04:26.040 --> 04:26.720
Let's go.

64
04:26.720 --> 04:27.440
Let's go.

65
04:28.360 --> 04:29.200
Stay away from me.

66
04:29.200 --> 04:29.800
You're such an embarrassment.

67
04:29.800 --> 04:31.120
It's such a narrow path.

68
04:31.120 --> 04:32.580
Where can I go to stay away?

69
04:33.120 --> 04:33.680
Mr. Wei.

70
04:34.640 --> 04:36.770
Is this salesman still in the company?

71
04:37.000 --> 04:37.880
Li Jinwang?

72
04:38.600 --> 04:40.480
He resigned two years ago

73
04:40.480 --> 04:41.720
and went back to his hometown.

74
04:41.720 --> 04:44.720
During his employment or around the time he left,

75
04:44.840 --> 04:47.240
did he have any conflicts with the company?

76
04:49.120 --> 04:49.920
Never.

77
04:50.000 --> 04:50.880
When he left,

78
04:50.880 --> 04:53.000
he was quite reluctant to leave this job.

79
04:53.000 --> 04:54.320
Because when he was here,

80
04:54.320 --> 04:57.520
his managers and colleagues were always very good to him.

81
04:58.320 --> 05:02.180
It's very disadvantageous for us that there's no sound in this video.

82
05:10.400 --> 05:12.320
Is this salesman still in the company?

83
05:12.320 --> 05:14.840
He was fired for taking kickbacks.

84
05:15.240 --> 05:18.440
I heard he went abroad and is basically unreachable.

85
05:29.480 --> 05:30.600
Okay.

86
05:34.600 --> 05:37.480
This Li Jinwang doesn't sound very cooperative.

87
05:37.920 --> 05:39.320
He's feeling guilty.

88
05:39.360 --> 05:41.720
Mr. Han said he didn't explain it fully,

89
05:41.720 --> 05:43.560
so he didn't fulfill what's it called,

90
05:43.560 --> 05:45.020
the obligation to inform.

91
05:45.040 --> 05:47.760
So we have to think carefully

92
05:48.240 --> 05:50.700
about how to persuade him to appear in court.

93
05:52.360 --> 05:53.040
Yes.

94
05:53.080 --> 05:54.080
Yes what?

95
05:54.080 --> 05:55.560
I'm asking you. Are you listening?

96
05:55.560 --> 05:56.280
I'm listening.

97
05:56.280 --> 05:57.080
Listening to what?

98
05:57.080 --> 05:59.480
My God, your yawns are almost like singing.

99
05:59.760 --> 06:00.600
I'm tired.

100
06:00.600 --> 06:02.000
I'm working hard.

101
06:02.000 --> 06:02.920
Don't fall asleep.

102
06:02.920 --> 06:03.800
We're on the highway.

103
06:03.800 --> 06:05.120
I still have dreams to realize.

104
06:05.120 --> 06:06.520
I don't want to die with you.

105
06:06.520 --> 06:07.160
How about this?

106
06:07.160 --> 06:08.120
Go to the service area ahead

107
06:08.120 --> 06:08.560
and park there.

108
06:08.560 --> 06:09.560
Let's take turns driving.

109
06:09.560 --> 06:10.760
You know how to drive?

110
06:10.800 --> 06:11.800
Mine is a manual.

111
06:12.400 --> 06:13.240
Who are you looking down on?

112
06:13.240 --> 06:14.760
My first car was a manual.

113
06:14.760 --> 06:16.090
"You know how to drive?"

114
06:16.560 --> 06:18.200
Then why did you stop driving?

115
06:18.200 --> 06:21.440
Well, I needed to raise money for the law firm,

116
06:21.920 --> 06:22.580
so I sold it.

117
06:22.600 --> 06:25.040
An old car is only worth a few thousand bucks now.

118
06:25.040 --> 06:26.440
You don't have to ride a little e-bike.

119
06:26.440 --> 06:27.280
What's wrong with an e-bike?

120
06:27.280 --> 06:28.200
It's flammable.

121
06:28.200 --> 06:30.400
It can take your life in just 30 seconds.

122
06:30.760 --> 06:32.400
That's why you're an amateur.

123
06:32.400 --> 06:34.520
What if I take a marriage or inheritance case?

124
06:34.520 --> 06:36.159
The clients can get so emotional.

125
06:36.159 --> 06:37.600
If they accidentally hurt the lawyer,

126
06:37.600 --> 06:40.040
I can just zoom away on my e-bike.

127
06:40.040 --> 06:40.880
How convenient is that?

128
06:40.880 --> 06:44.480
Convenient for running away? How many people have you offended?

129
06:45.040 --> 06:47.760
Why exactly did you leave the big firm?

130
06:47.800 --> 06:49.200
To put it simply,

131
06:50.320 --> 06:51.040
it's just

132
06:52.960 --> 06:53.960
a clash of values.

133
06:54.440 --> 06:56.159
That's why we get along.

134
06:56.159 --> 06:57.320
I don't get along with them either.

135
06:57.320 --> 06:58.240
Especially that Li Xiang,

136
06:58.240 --> 06:59.040
he's so pretentious.

137
06:59.040 --> 07:00.040
Not only do our values clash,

138
07:00.040 --> 07:01.160
but our features clash.

139
07:01.160 --> 07:02.760
Every organ in our bodies clashes.

140
07:02.760 --> 07:04.880
There aren't many people who get along with you.

141
07:04.880 --> 07:05.960
We get along.

142
07:05.960 --> 07:07.760
How do I get along with you? My goodness.

143
07:07.760 --> 07:09.640
The enemy of my enemy is my friend.

144
07:09.640 --> 07:10.840
Neither of us gets along with him.

145
07:10.840 --> 07:12.600
Don't drag me down with you.

146
07:12.600 --> 07:14.080
Your head is just a bit rounder than mine.

147
07:14.080 --> 07:15.520
Otherwise, we look pretty much the same.

148
07:15.520 --> 07:16.880
My goodness, just focus on driving.

149
07:16.880 --> 07:17.520
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

150
07:17.520 --> 07:18.720
There, there, there.

151
07:19.640 --> 07:20.400
Mentor,

152
07:20.600 --> 07:23.160
if Li Jinwang testifies for the plaintiff in court,

153
07:23.160 --> 07:25.220
will it put us at a huge disadvantage?

154
07:25.720 --> 07:26.280
Yes.

155
07:26.800 --> 07:27.680
Verdicts in insurance cases

156
07:27.680 --> 07:29.520
naturally tend to favor the weaker party.

157
07:29.520 --> 07:31.850
So we have to get there before Xiao Longnv.

158
07:33.640 --> 07:34.640
By the way, Ruoqi,

159
07:35.120 --> 07:36.650
did you bring a plastic bag?

160
07:38.960 --> 07:39.760
A file folder.

161
07:40.640 --> 07:41.640
Thank you, Mr. Li.

162
07:43.320 --> 07:44.250
You're quite...

163
07:45.440 --> 07:47.240
Throw up less. Don't let it leak.

164
07:54.640 --> 07:56.200
I threw up all my breakfast.

165
07:56.320 --> 07:58.580
If you can't handle it, I'll drive later.

166
08:01.200 --> 08:03.460
What a coincidence. Where are you going?

167
08:04.640 --> 08:05.840
Why didn't you wash your hands,

168
08:05.840 --> 08:06.320
boss?

169
08:07.080 --> 08:08.280
That's really dirty.

170
08:09.040 --> 08:10.080
Go, go, go.

171
08:10.520 --> 08:11.520
What's wrong? What happened?

172
08:11.520 --> 08:12.780
Is a ghost chasing you?

173
08:13.000 --> 08:14.680
The people from Honghu are here too.

174
08:14.680 --> 08:15.480
Get in the car.

175
08:15.480 --> 08:16.680
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

176
08:16.800 --> 08:17.730
Perfect timing.

177
08:17.840 --> 08:18.320
Come on,

178
08:18.720 --> 08:19.840
shouldn't we deal with them?

179
08:19.840 --> 08:20.280
Let's deal with them.

180
08:20.280 --> 08:20.520
Come on.

181
08:20.520 --> 08:21.650
One, two, three, go.

182
08:22.760 --> 08:24.400
Release the handbrake.

183
08:24.520 --> 08:25.840
I'm a bit rusty.

184
08:26.040 --> 08:26.800
Wait a minute, Mr. Li.

185
08:26.800 --> 08:27.400
I feel a bit nauseous.

186
08:27.400 --> 08:29.400
Let me throw up again. Just a second.

187
08:30.560 --> 08:31.560
Go, go, go.

188
08:33.559 --> 08:35.120
No, no, no. Don't start in third gear.

189
08:35.120 --> 08:37.039
How can you drive off at 4,000 RPM?

190
08:37.640 --> 08:38.760
You need to coordinate the clutch and gas.

191
08:38.760 --> 08:39.320
Slow down a bit.

192
08:39.320 --> 08:40.640
My car can't take this.

193
08:40.640 --> 08:41.440
Don't do this.

194
08:41.440 --> 08:42.039
Do you know how to drive?

195
08:42.039 --> 08:44.039
Slow down. You'll ruin the car.

196
08:45.760 --> 08:46.880
Can you give it a rest?

197
08:46.880 --> 08:49.340
You're affecting my performance, you know?

198
08:51.840 --> 08:53.400
That's it. Nice and steady.

199
08:53.400 --> 08:55.800
It's just overtaking a Mercedes. Let's go.

200
09:17.520 --> 09:19.120
You're driving pretty fast.

201
09:20.720 --> 09:21.360
Move.

202
09:22.080 --> 09:23.210
Why are you pushing?

203
09:27.920 --> 09:28.720
Is it ready yet, boss?

204
09:28.720 --> 09:29.040
Number 29. 29.

205
09:29.040 --> 09:30.840
Brother Li, Brother Li. You're Brother Li, right?

206
09:30.840 --> 09:32.520
What are you doing? Can't you see we're in line?

207
09:32.520 --> 09:33.400
Everyone's in a hurry. Get in the back.

208
09:33.400 --> 09:33.840
No.

209
09:34.080 --> 09:35.400
It's fine. Brother Li,

210
09:35.440 --> 09:36.960
I'm Han Zhenhua's lawyer.

211
09:36.960 --> 09:38.040
We just talked on the phone.

212
09:38.040 --> 09:38.760
Hello, Mr. Li.

213
09:38.760 --> 09:40.120
I'm the lawyer for Shengkang Insurance.

214
09:40.120 --> 09:40.920
I'm Su Bowen.

215
09:40.920 --> 09:41.880
This is my colleague.

216
09:41.880 --> 09:43.040
Saying hello is useless. Come on.

217
09:43.040 --> 09:43.920
Brother Li, are you busy?

218
09:43.920 --> 09:44.920
Let me help you chop.

219
09:44.920 --> 09:45.600
You're so dirty.

220
09:45.600 --> 09:46.440
What are you chopping?

221
09:46.440 --> 09:47.240
Do you have a health certificate?

222
09:47.240 --> 09:49.000
What? Bite me. I don't have a health certificate.

223
09:49.000 --> 09:50.120
You're covered in bacteria, you know?

224
09:50.120 --> 09:50.760
Boss, here's the thing.

225
09:50.760 --> 09:51.880
Try pushing again.

226
09:52.160 --> 09:53.440
What? Lawyers don't have to wait in line?

227
09:53.440 --> 09:54.560
Everyone, everyone, everyone.

228
09:54.560 --> 09:55.840
I'm busy getting orders out right now.

229
09:55.840 --> 09:56.880
I don't have time to entertain you.

230
09:56.880 --> 09:58.000
Hurry up, boss. It's going to time out.

231
09:58.000 --> 09:58.960
Right away, right away, right away.

232
09:58.960 --> 09:59.760
Brother Li, how about this?

233
09:59.760 --> 10:00.880
After you finish these two orders,

234
10:00.880 --> 10:02.280
don't make the rest for now.

235
10:02.280 --> 10:03.120
Let's have a chat.

236
10:03.120 --> 10:04.640
I'll compensate you for the loss. How about that?

237
10:04.640 --> 10:05.800
Yes, we can pay double.

238
10:05.800 --> 10:06.880
Is this an auction? Paying double?

239
10:06.880 --> 10:07.640
Showing off your money?

240
10:07.640 --> 10:09.640
Brother Li, is the original price okay? I'm begging you.

241
10:09.640 --> 10:11.040
It's not about the money.

242
10:11.400 --> 10:12.730
I'm very busy right now.

243
10:13.600 --> 10:14.400
Leave.

244
10:15.600 --> 10:17.000
Don't crowd my shop.

245
10:18.880 --> 10:19.880
Just go.

246
10:20.280 --> 10:21.680
Don't crowd their shop.

247
10:22.360 --> 10:23.480
Boss, serve us first.

248
10:23.480 --> 10:24.340
Get out of here.

249
10:35.000 --> 10:35.880
Mr. Li.

250
10:36.200 --> 10:38.280
When the time comes, you just need to

251
10:38.280 --> 10:40.040
explain the signing process in court.

252
10:40.040 --> 10:41.320
Mr. Li, I am obligated to inform you

253
10:41.320 --> 10:42.280
that if you, at that time,

254
10:42.280 --> 10:43.920
failed to fulfill your duty to inform,

255
10:43.920 --> 10:45.040
the insurance company

256
10:45.040 --> 10:46.280
might hold you accountable later.

257
10:46.280 --> 10:47.200
Don't listen to his nonsense.

258
10:47.200 --> 10:48.280
Mr. Li, they won't.

259
10:48.360 --> 10:49.800
Since the time of signing,

260
10:49.800 --> 10:50.920
the statute of limitations has passed.

261
10:50.920 --> 10:52.280
It absolutely won't affect you.

262
10:52.280 --> 10:52.920
Mr. Li.

263
10:52.920 --> 10:54.200
You must make sure your testimony

264
10:54.200 --> 10:55.440
is 100% true.

265
10:55.440 --> 10:56.520
Once in court,

266
10:56.560 --> 10:58.520
if your testimony doesn't match the facts,

267
10:58.520 --> 11:00.280
you may bear

268
11:00.440 --> 11:02.160
criminal responsibility for perjury.

269
11:02.160 --> 11:02.400
No.

270
11:02.400 --> 11:04.960
Are you threatening the witness not to testify?

271
11:04.960 --> 11:06.280
I'm telling Mr. Li

272
11:06.280 --> 11:08.080
what he should pay attention to.

273
11:08.400 --> 11:10.730
Lawyers, please don't make it hard for me.

274
11:11.320 --> 11:12.640
I used to work at Shengkang Insurance,

275
11:12.640 --> 11:14.040
and the boss treated me well.

276
11:14.040 --> 11:16.040
I sold Mr. Han's insurance.

277
11:16.600 --> 11:18.080
Now that there's a problem,

278
11:18.080 --> 11:19.280
I feel terrible too.

279
11:19.880 --> 11:20.920
If we go to court,

280
11:21.040 --> 11:21.920
how can I face

281
11:22.400 --> 11:23.200
both sides?

282
11:23.360 --> 11:26.360
What you should face most are the facts and the truth.

283
11:28.080 --> 11:30.540
You should be very familiar with this photo.

284
11:33.840 --> 11:35.320
We are all parents.

285
11:35.440 --> 11:37.840
Shouldn't we put ourselves in their shoes?

286
11:47.680 --> 11:49.810
This little motorcycle can even move.

287
12:05.080 --> 12:06.840
You're quite tall, sis. Are you 1.8 meters?

288
12:06.840 --> 12:07.600
I'm not.

289
12:08.200 --> 12:09.600
Just talk. Don't lean over here.

290
12:09.600 --> 12:10.600
Move over there.

291
12:10.840 --> 12:12.160
Harassing my female colleague over there.

292
12:12.160 --> 12:13.200
Then sue me.

293
12:13.360 --> 12:14.800
What's harassment? What's small talk?

294
12:14.800 --> 12:15.760
Can't you tell?

295
12:15.760 --> 12:16.880
Just throwing words around.

296
12:16.880 --> 12:18.000
I think you look quite tacky.

297
12:18.000 --> 12:19.120
Calling people 'sis' all day long.

298
12:19.120 --> 12:20.520
Aren't you tacky?

299
12:20.880 --> 12:22.760
Do you know what's tacky and what's trendy?

300
12:22.760 --> 12:23.640
Look at your hairstyle.

301
12:23.640 --> 12:24.360
I'm warning you.

302
12:24.360 --> 12:25.440
Don't talk about my hairstyle.

303
12:25.440 --> 12:27.400
Your hairstyle looks like parentheses. So what if I said it?

304
12:27.400 --> 12:28.400
You're one to talk.

305
12:28.400 --> 12:29.920
Look at your alternative mullet.

306
12:29.920 --> 12:31.880
You're wearing your uncle's clothes.

307
12:31.880 --> 12:32.640
My old...

308
12:32.640 --> 12:33.280
How is it?

309
12:33.520 --> 12:34.520
What do you think?

310
12:34.560 --> 12:35.640
Absolutely. Understood.

311
12:35.640 --> 12:36.970
Let's go. Get in the car.

312
12:40.240 --> 12:41.520
Lawyer Li, how did it go?

313
12:41.520 --> 12:43.580
Why even ask? Look how arrogant he is.

314
12:44.400 --> 12:44.880
No, no way.

315
12:44.880 --> 12:46.610
I'll go in and talk to him again.

316
12:47.360 --> 12:48.640
No need. Get in the car.

317
12:52.000 --> 12:53.860
Bluetooth, help me find someone.

318
12:59.040 --> 13:01.120
Your case goes to trial today, right?

319
13:03.480 --> 13:06.560
Yeah, right here. I think you're a little nervous.

320
13:07.240 --> 13:08.120
Why would I be nervous?

321
13:08.120 --> 13:09.040
We've known each other for so many years.

322
13:09.040 --> 13:10.880
It's not our first time being opponents.

323
13:10.880 --> 13:12.610
We've done so many mock trials.

324
13:12.880 --> 13:14.920
I meant your muscles are tense.

325
13:15.160 --> 13:16.690
What are you talking about?

326
13:17.200 --> 13:18.930
I was talking about my muscles.

327
13:19.000 --> 13:20.730
I've been in court a lot lately.

328
13:20.800 --> 13:21.930
My jaw is a bit tight.

329
13:22.040 --> 13:23.720
And my facial muscles are a bit tense.

330
13:23.720 --> 13:25.640
Okay, I'll loosen you up in a bit.

331
13:26.600 --> 13:28.400
How? By slapping me twice?

332
13:29.000 --> 13:29.720
Relax.

333
13:30.280 --> 13:31.520
Gently.

334
13:37.400 --> 13:38.680
Come on.

335
13:43.760 --> 13:44.280
What?

336
13:44.320 --> 13:45.480
What are you looking at?

337
13:45.480 --> 13:46.680
Eat your food.

338
13:47.320 --> 13:48.280
So much?

339
13:48.280 --> 13:49.520
I'm cheering you on.

340
13:49.520 --> 13:51.000
You need a full stomach to fight well. Come on.

341
13:51.000 --> 13:53.800
Don't show him any mercy this time.

342
13:53.800 --> 13:54.880
But don't be too harsh either.

343
13:54.880 --> 13:55.520
Men.

344
13:55.520 --> 13:57.520
Sometimes they can't handle losing face.

345
13:57.520 --> 13:59.180
Okay, I'll fight how I should.

346
13:59.360 --> 14:00.420
Where are the buns?

347
14:00.560 --> 14:01.690
They're still warm.

348
14:01.760 --> 14:02.680
I'll take them then.

349
14:02.680 --> 14:03.480
What for?

350
14:03.800 --> 14:04.640
Just eat them.

351
14:04.640 --> 14:05.400
Eat before you go.

352
14:05.400 --> 14:07.000
Be safe. Safety first.

353
14:07.400 --> 14:08.160
I'm leaving.

354
14:10.360 --> 14:11.290
Let's make a bet.

355
14:11.680 --> 14:13.400
I'm definitely betting on Xiaolong.

356
14:13.400 --> 14:14.920
Why would you bet on her?

357
14:15.400 --> 14:16.800
That's your own son.

358
14:17.400 --> 14:18.400
He bought you sea cucumbers for nothing.

359
14:18.400 --> 14:20.260
Besides, didn't you eat them too?

360
14:22.600 --> 14:23.530
I bet on Xiaoxin.

361
15:03.080 --> 15:04.680
The court investigation phase is over.

362
15:04.680 --> 15:06.120
We now enter the debate phase.

363
15:06.120 --> 15:10.120
First, the plaintiff's representative will present their arguments.

364
15:10.520 --> 15:11.320
Your Honor.

365
15:11.920 --> 15:14.480
According to the regulations promulgated by the National Financial Regulatory Administration

366
15:14.480 --> 15:16.800
in the "Health Insurance Management Measures",

367
15:16.800 --> 15:18.680
insurance companies shall not use diagnostic criteria

368
15:18.680 --> 15:20.880
that do not match the insurance contract as a reason

369
15:20.880 --> 15:22.480
to refuse to pay insurance benefits.

370
15:22.480 --> 15:23.160
Regarding this case,

371
15:23.160 --> 15:25.800
for the condition of disseminated intravascular coagulation,

372
15:25.800 --> 15:27.440
whether it has early, middle, or late stages,

373
15:27.440 --> 15:29.200
and whether a blood transfusion was required as a result,

374
15:29.200 --> 15:31.120
it is all because the hospital and the insurance company have

375
15:31.120 --> 15:32.480
different diagnostic criteria.

376
15:32.480 --> 15:35.440
Therefore, the defendant cannot refuse to pay on this basis.

377
15:35.440 --> 15:36.120
Your Honor.

378
15:36.120 --> 15:37.880
The National Financial Regulatory Administration is an agency

379
15:37.880 --> 15:40.240
that supervises the banking and insurance industries.

380
15:40.240 --> 15:42.560
It does not have any law enforcement power.

381
15:42.560 --> 15:44.880
I believe the regulations presented by the plaintiff's lawyer

382
15:44.880 --> 15:47.880
are too broad in scope

383
15:47.960 --> 15:49.680
to be directly used as a basis for judgment.

384
15:49.680 --> 15:51.400
However, the National Financial Regulatory Administration

385
15:51.400 --> 15:52.720
issued such a regulation

386
15:52.720 --> 15:53.480
for a reason.

387
15:53.800 --> 15:54.680
For fairness.

388
15:55.600 --> 15:56.600
As we all know,

389
15:56.760 --> 15:59.040
insurance companies have so many departments,

390
15:59.040 --> 16:00.160
so many employees,

391
16:00.360 --> 16:02.440
and so many top legal advisors.

392
16:02.520 --> 16:04.720
They exhaust every means every day

393
16:04.720 --> 16:07.040
to add various details to the policies.

394
16:07.280 --> 16:09.720
A policy can have hundreds of pages.

395
16:10.280 --> 16:12.800
Most of the content is obscure and difficult to understand.

396
16:12.800 --> 16:15.280
It takes a law student several days to read it,

397
16:15.280 --> 16:16.940
let alone an ordinary person.

398
16:17.120 --> 16:19.720
They simply cannot finish reading or understand it.

399
16:19.720 --> 16:22.280
Nor is it possible to get sick according to the contents of the policy.

400
16:22.280 --> 16:22.920
Plaintiff.

401
16:22.920 --> 16:23.400
What is DIC (disseminated intravascular coagulation)

402
16:23.400 --> 16:23.960
exactly?

403
16:24.680 --> 16:25.200
How many stages does DIC (disseminated intravascular coagulation)

404
16:25.200 --> 16:26.040
have?

405
16:26.320 --> 16:29.200
Even someone who has studied medicine has to look it up in a textbook.

406
16:29.200 --> 16:30.080
But now,

407
16:30.400 --> 16:31.800
as an ordinary person,

408
16:31.800 --> 16:34.040
to get compensation from an insurance company,

409
16:34.040 --> 16:35.840
one must master this knowledge.

410
16:36.800 --> 16:37.720
It's like

411
16:38.160 --> 16:40.560
a rich kid driving a sports car

412
16:40.800 --> 16:43.800
wanting to race an ordinary person walking on foot.

413
16:44.200 --> 16:46.920
Yes, an ordinary person would definitely lose.

414
16:47.920 --> 16:49.040
But is that fair?

415
16:50.200 --> 16:50.920
Your Honor,

416
16:51.320 --> 16:52.280
I believe the plaintiff's lawyer

417
16:52.280 --> 16:54.080
used an inappropriate example.

418
16:54.200 --> 16:56.560
As a professional insurance institution,

419
16:56.560 --> 17:00.080
we serve the vast majority of ordinary people.

420
17:00.520 --> 17:03.200
Every salesperson undergoes professional

421
17:03.200 --> 17:05.260
and standardized pre-job training.

422
17:05.680 --> 17:06.800
For every client,

423
17:06.800 --> 17:08.560
we have reception videos

424
17:08.560 --> 17:10.819
and after-sales follow-up recordings.

425
17:10.920 --> 17:11.800
The purpose of doing this

426
17:11.800 --> 17:13.920
is precisely to make up for

427
17:13.920 --> 17:17.720
the so-called unfairness raised by the plaintiff.

428
17:18.079 --> 17:20.240
To borrow the plaintiff's lawyer's example,

429
17:20.240 --> 17:22.300
the company uses these requirements

430
17:22.440 --> 17:26.369
to bring ordinary people into the sports car to move forward together.

431
17:26.680 --> 17:29.280
What nonsense. What sports car can fit so many people?

432
17:29.280 --> 17:30.120
Uncle, it's a metaphor.

433
17:30.120 --> 17:30.880
Your Honor,

434
17:31.000 --> 17:31.560
I know.

435
17:31.560 --> 17:33.600
In response to the argument just raised by the defense,

436
17:33.600 --> 17:35.960
I request that the former salesperson who signed the insurance contract,

437
17:35.960 --> 17:38.920
Li Jinwang, appear in court as a witness.

438
17:40.000 --> 17:40.720
Granted.

439
17:40.920 --> 17:43.120
Summon witness Li Jinwang to the court.

440
17:50.240 --> 17:52.700
The plaintiff may now question the witness.

441
17:53.120 --> 17:53.960
Li Jinwang,

442
17:54.160 --> 17:56.800
before signing the contract, did you explain to the plaintiff,

443
17:56.800 --> 17:58.320
who is my client,

444
17:58.400 --> 18:00.640
all the terms of the contract,

445
18:00.640 --> 18:03.440
all the diseases, and the related restrictions?

446
18:04.720 --> 18:05.600
On the day of signing,

447
18:05.600 --> 18:08.120
I was explaining the contract to Mr. Han and the others,

448
18:08.120 --> 18:10.600
telling them that they could ask me

449
18:10.600 --> 18:12.000
about any parts they had doubts about.

450
18:12.000 --> 18:12.720
But suddenly,

451
18:12.720 --> 18:14.980
I received a call from my father-in-law,

452
18:15.120 --> 18:16.720
saying my wife was about to give birth.

453
18:16.720 --> 18:17.840
So I went out to answer the phone.

454
18:17.840 --> 18:18.840
In other words,

455
18:19.360 --> 18:21.600
you didn't thoroughly explain the contents of the contract

456
18:21.600 --> 18:23.360
that day, right?

457
18:26.520 --> 18:29.580
Right. After the call, I went back to the reception room

458
18:29.600 --> 18:32.200
and explained the situation to Mr. Han and the others.

459
18:32.200 --> 18:33.840
They congratulated me

460
18:33.840 --> 18:35.500
and didn't ask anything else.

461
18:35.680 --> 18:37.560
I signed the contract

462
18:39.400 --> 18:40.600
and left the company.

463
18:40.960 --> 18:43.220
Your Honor, I have no further questions.

464
18:43.880 --> 18:44.640
Your Honor,

465
18:44.720 --> 18:47.120
I also have some questions for the witness.

466
18:49.560 --> 18:52.200
Mr. Li, regarding the situation four years ago,

467
18:52.200 --> 18:54.130
can you still remember it clearly?

468
19:07.440 --> 19:08.000
Yes.

469
19:08.320 --> 19:10.480
Because that was the day my child was born,

470
19:10.480 --> 19:12.480
I remember what happened very clearly.

471
19:12.480 --> 19:14.160
Could you please clarify

472
19:14.160 --> 19:16.880
the parts you explained and didn't explain?

473
19:17.600 --> 19:19.920
Regarding the basic parts trained by the company,

474
19:19.920 --> 19:22.000
I gave a detailed explanation at that time.

475
19:22.000 --> 19:23.400
Next, the clients needed to

476
19:23.400 --> 19:25.600
ask questions about the unclear parts,

477
19:25.960 --> 19:27.360
and we would answer them.

478
19:27.520 --> 19:30.720
But due to my personal reasons, this was not completed.

479
19:30.880 --> 19:32.040
So, in other words,

480
19:32.880 --> 19:36.440
regarding the basic contract details trained by the company,

481
19:36.480 --> 19:38.280
you had already finished explaining them.

482
19:38.280 --> 19:39.520
It was only when the clients wanted to

483
19:39.520 --> 19:41.640
ask further questions about their own situations

484
19:41.640 --> 19:43.640
that you left the reception room, right?

485
19:43.640 --> 19:44.200
Yes.

486
19:44.720 --> 19:45.440
Your Honor,

487
19:47.440 --> 19:47.640
I...

488
19:47.640 --> 19:48.720
the video evidence from the reception room submitted earlier...

489
19:48.720 --> 19:49.080
I...

490
19:49.080 --> 19:49.800
the video evidence from the reception room submitted earlier,

491
19:49.800 --> 19:51.840
I would like to further elaborate on it.

492
19:51.840 --> 19:53.800
Granted. Please play it.

493
20:18.880 --> 20:19.480
Mr. Han.

494
20:20.280 --> 20:21.080
What's wrong?

495
20:23.880 --> 20:27.440
After Mr. Li Jinwang left the reception room in the video,

496
20:28.040 --> 20:29.520
the lady who came in

497
20:29.800 --> 20:32.600
was also a salesperson for Shengkang Insurance at the time.

498
20:32.600 --> 20:33.920
Mr. and Mrs. Han

499
20:34.080 --> 20:37.000
questioned this salesperson,

500
20:37.480 --> 20:39.320
and she gave a detailed answer.

501
20:39.520 --> 20:40.240
Your Honor,

502
20:40.240 --> 20:41.400
the video has no sound.

503
20:41.400 --> 20:42.120
It cannot be proven

504
20:42.120 --> 20:44.080
that the salesperson was explaining

505
20:44.080 --> 20:45.600
the contract details to my client.

506
20:45.600 --> 20:47.130
Counsel for the defendant,

507
20:47.320 --> 20:48.200
can your salesperson

508
20:48.200 --> 20:49.960
also appear in court to testify?

509
20:49.960 --> 20:50.620
Your Honor,

510
20:50.920 --> 20:52.760
the salesperson has resigned

511
20:52.760 --> 20:54.040
and is not in the country.

512
20:54.040 --> 20:55.840
But we have hired a lip-reading expert

513
20:55.840 --> 20:57.920
to translate the video evidence.

514
20:57.920 --> 20:59.380
And it has been notarized.

515
20:59.440 --> 21:02.440
We can submit it together as supplementary evidence.

516
21:05.480 --> 21:08.480
Counsel for the plaintiff, please take a look as well.

517
21:12.000 --> 21:13.440
After expert analysis,

518
21:13.440 --> 21:14.720
the content of this video

519
21:14.720 --> 21:15.000
between the video evidence and witness testimony, exactly shows Mr. Han asking the salesperson in the surveillance video provided by the applicant.

520
21:15.000 --> 21:17.400
exactly shows Mr. Han asking the salesperson

521
21:17.400 --> 21:20.040
under what conditions the policy would be denied,

522
21:20.040 --> 21:21.440
and she gave an answer.

523
21:21.680 --> 21:24.920
If it does not meet the policy's disease restrictions,

524
21:24.920 --> 21:27.200
such as severe coma resuscitation

525
21:27.200 --> 21:30.240
for less than 96 hours, it will be denied.

526
21:32.200 --> 21:33.520
I really forgot.

527
21:34.120 --> 21:36.600
There was too much said, and it was too complicated at the time.

528
21:36.600 --> 21:38.840
I... I really forgot.

529
21:46.440 --> 21:47.760
Our insurance company

530
21:47.920 --> 21:50.280
has fulfilled its obligation to inform.

531
21:50.400 --> 21:51.040
And the plaintiff,

532
21:51.040 --> 21:54.080
knowing that 96 hours of resuscitation was required

533
21:54.080 --> 21:56.000
to receive compensation,

534
21:56.000 --> 21:58.440
still actively chose to give up,

535
21:58.640 --> 22:01.840
and later filed a lawsuit against the insurance company.

536
22:03.480 --> 22:06.210
This is a violation of the spirit of the contract.

537
22:07.440 --> 22:09.560
We will now proceed to closing statements.

538
22:09.560 --> 22:12.290
Proceed in the order of plaintiff and defendant.

539
22:13.560 --> 22:14.640
My clients

540
22:15.520 --> 22:17.960
are parents who have just lost their child.

541
22:18.320 --> 22:19.600
Like millions of

542
22:19.600 --> 22:20.920
ordinary people,

543
22:21.000 --> 22:24.120
they have no professional knowledge of medicine or insurance.

544
22:24.120 --> 22:25.680
They cannot clearly understand

545
22:25.680 --> 22:28.840
under what circumstances they qualify for compensation,

546
22:28.840 --> 22:31.100
or which specific conditions they meet.

547
22:31.160 --> 22:32.220
But the defendant,

548
22:32.960 --> 22:34.560
a professional institution,

549
22:34.560 --> 22:36.640
should have explained it in detail beforehand,

550
22:36.640 --> 22:39.400
and actively contacted the clients afterwards

551
22:39.480 --> 22:42.280
to identify the items and basis for compensation.

552
22:42.400 --> 22:44.000
Instead of acting like this,

553
22:44.000 --> 22:46.920
taking advantage of the clients' lack of knowledge

554
22:47.080 --> 22:49.810
to evade responsibility and coldly reject them.

555
22:50.840 --> 22:51.560
Finally,

556
22:51.800 --> 22:52.760
I would like to

557
22:53.440 --> 22:55.720
address the issue repeatedly raised by the opposing counsel

558
22:55.720 --> 22:56.980
and provide an answer.

559
22:58.040 --> 23:00.000
I hope you can tell me the truth.

560
23:00.760 --> 23:01.880
At that time,

561
23:02.880 --> 23:05.610
why did you voluntarily stop the resuscitation?

562
23:07.440 --> 23:08.240
At that time,

563
23:09.960 --> 23:10.720
Xinxin had already been

564
23:10.720 --> 23:11.560
in the ICU

565
23:14.320 --> 23:17.120
undergoing emergency treatment for forty hours.

566
23:24.040 --> 23:25.960
Director Lin, how is my Xinxin?

567
23:25.960 --> 23:27.320
Don't worry.

568
23:27.320 --> 23:28.440
Calm down.

569
23:28.840 --> 23:30.760
Xinxin's father, come with me.

570
24:01.000 --> 24:02.920
What happened to Xinxin's chest?

571
24:08.880 --> 24:09.520
Xinxin,

572
24:12.000 --> 24:13.040
does it hurt?

573
24:13.960 --> 24:14.840
Han Kexin,

574
24:15.520 --> 24:16.920
such a young child.

575
24:17.440 --> 24:18.240
Her chest

576
24:18.960 --> 24:21.520
caved in from chest compressions.

577
24:21.920 --> 24:23.280
Five ribs were broken,

578
24:23.760 --> 24:25.560
and she could no longer be saved.

579
24:31.200 --> 24:33.920
Her parents gave up on treatment.

580
24:36.000 --> 24:38.260
It's not because they want to save money.

581
24:38.480 --> 24:39.480
At that moment,

582
24:39.480 --> 24:41.440
they couldn't possibly be thinking about

583
24:41.440 --> 24:43.320
whether they would get compensated or not.

584
24:43.320 --> 24:44.840
Let's go home and sleep.

585
24:48.280 --> 24:50.720
Hold on a little longer. We're going home.

586
24:51.760 --> 24:53.000
They just hope

587
24:53.200 --> 24:55.530
that their child can go home one more time,

588
24:56.760 --> 24:59.080
return to her favorite little bed,

589
25:03.040 --> 25:04.240
and leave this world.

590
25:08.840 --> 25:10.240
Since the child's death,

591
25:10.600 --> 25:11.720
the parents

592
25:11.800 --> 25:14.400
have not been able to recover from their grief.

593
25:14.800 --> 25:18.480
Insurance shouldn't just be a cold contract.

594
25:19.120 --> 25:20.850
It should be a responsibility,

595
25:21.480 --> 25:24.760
care, and a promise.

596
25:25.960 --> 25:26.720
That is all.

597
25:28.000 --> 25:29.720
We maintain our claim.

598
25:30.560 --> 25:33.080
The defendant may make their final statement.

599
25:33.080 --> 25:35.880
Regarding what Mr. and Mrs. Han have been through,

600
25:38.960 --> 25:39.960
I am deeply sorry.

601
26:01.560 --> 26:02.520
Insurance

602
26:03.600 --> 26:05.200
is meant to serve the public.

603
26:05.480 --> 26:06.720
But the public

604
26:07.120 --> 26:09.920
is made up of all kinds of individuals.

605
26:10.280 --> 26:12.810
That's why legal constraints are necessary.

606
26:12.920 --> 26:15.840
And the essence of insurance is a legal contract.

607
26:16.440 --> 26:19.600
The spirit of contract is the key to establishing its long-term reliability

608
26:19.600 --> 26:22.720
and achieving stability in transaction order.

609
26:23.600 --> 26:25.280
If we arbitrarily break

610
26:26.000 --> 26:28.060
the limits of the insurance contract

611
26:28.120 --> 26:30.720
and use emotional factors to force the insurance company

612
26:30.720 --> 26:31.760
to pay out,

613
26:32.360 --> 26:35.040
it may seem like we are upholding justice for an individual case,

614
26:35.040 --> 26:37.200
but in reality, we are destroying

615
26:37.200 --> 26:39.860
the foundation of trust in the entire industry.

616
26:40.360 --> 26:41.480
Then in the future, for all

617
26:41.480 --> 26:42.560
diseases that do not meet the definition,

618
26:42.560 --> 26:44.000
do we have to pay out?

619
26:44.680 --> 26:45.920
How should we pay out?

620
26:45.920 --> 26:46.920
In what way?

621
26:47.000 --> 26:47.920
How much?

622
26:49.240 --> 26:50.120
It will lead to chaos in the industry.

623
26:50.120 --> 26:51.680
It will inevitably lead to chaos in the industry

624
26:51.680 --> 26:54.140
and destroy the foundation of the industry.

625
26:54.440 --> 26:54.920
In fact,

626
26:54.920 --> 26:57.380
for every unreasonable individual payout,

627
26:57.520 --> 26:59.720
all these children's critical illness insurance policies on the market

628
26:59.720 --> 27:01.920
will have to undergo a new round of price adjustments.

629
27:01.920 --> 27:04.120
They will all have to increase in price.

630
27:04.520 --> 27:06.920
And who will ultimately suffer from this?

631
27:07.360 --> 27:08.560
It will still be these

632
27:08.560 --> 27:10.560
ordinary people who need to be protected.

633
27:10.560 --> 27:11.880
It will still be these

634
27:11.880 --> 27:13.880
families who need to be protected.

635
27:14.680 --> 27:16.480
Therefore, we implore the court

636
27:17.360 --> 27:19.290
to dismiss the plaintiff's claim.

637
27:24.880 --> 27:25.880
All rise.

638
27:27.200 --> 27:29.400
The verdict for this case will now be announced.

639
27:29.400 --> 27:30.520
This court holds that

640
27:30.520 --> 27:32.840
in this case, the insurer, regarding the insurance contract's

641
27:32.840 --> 27:35.600
concept of the clause exempting the insurer's liability,

642
27:35.600 --> 27:37.680
its content, and its legal consequences,

643
27:37.680 --> 27:40.120
has provided the policyholder in written and oral forms

644
27:40.120 --> 27:43.080
with an explanation that an ordinary person can understand.

645
27:43.080 --> 27:45.360
According to Judicial Interpretation II of the Insurance Law,

646
27:45.360 --> 27:46.520
Article 11,

647
27:46.560 --> 27:47.280
it should be deemed

648
27:47.280 --> 27:49.560
to have fulfilled the

649
27:49.560 --> 27:51.440
explicit explanation obligation stipulated in the Insurance Law.

650
27:51.440 --> 27:53.840
The insurance contract involved in the case uses an enumerative method.

651
27:53.840 --> 27:55.680
The types of critical illnesses covered by the insurance

652
27:55.680 --> 27:56.720
have been stipulated,

653
27:56.720 --> 27:57.800
which are clear and specific,

654
27:57.800 --> 28:00.080
and there is no difference in understanding.

655
28:00.080 --> 28:00.880
Accordingly,

656
28:00.880 --> 28:03.080
in accordance with the Civil Code of the People's Republic of China,

657
28:03.080 --> 28:05.200
Article 509, Paragraph 2,

658
28:05.200 --> 28:07.080
and the Insurance Law of the People's Republic of China,

659
28:07.080 --> 28:08.680
Article 14,

660
28:09.200 --> 28:10.640
the judgment is as follows:

661
28:10.640 --> 28:13.500
The plaintiff Han Zhenhua's claims are dismissed.

662
28:13.760 --> 28:15.400
If you disagree with this judgment,

663
28:15.400 --> 28:18.200
you may, within 15 days from the date of receiving the judgment,

664
28:18.200 --> 28:19.960
file an appeal with this court

665
28:20.320 --> 28:23.160
and submit copies of the appeal petition according to the number of parties involved,

666
28:23.160 --> 28:25.320
appealing to the Leyang City

667
28:25.320 --> 28:26.880
Intermediate People's Court of Fengan Province.

668
28:26.880 --> 28:28.240
Court is adjourned.

669
28:38.440 --> 28:39.200
I'm sorry.

670
28:40.120 --> 28:41.400
I really forgot

671
28:42.480 --> 28:44.240
what that salesman told me.

672
28:45.560 --> 28:47.890
Mr. Han, you don't need to blame yourself.

673
28:49.200 --> 28:50.720
For cases like this,

674
28:52.000 --> 28:54.800
every judge has a different standard of judgment.

675
28:54.960 --> 28:56.720
If we continue to appeal,

676
28:57.520 --> 28:58.880
we might still win.

677
28:59.400 --> 29:00.240
As long as you want,

678
29:00.240 --> 29:01.880
I can handle the appeal for you.

679
29:01.880 --> 29:03.720
Right, let's keep fighting.

680
29:04.240 --> 29:05.440
Let's stop here.

681
29:10.120 --> 29:11.680
After our Xinxin left us,

682
29:12.440 --> 29:13.680
I feel like

683
29:15.400 --> 29:17.800
I've just been following others every day.

684
29:18.280 --> 29:20.680
Her dad said he wanted to claim compensation,

685
29:20.680 --> 29:22.280
so I followed him to claim it.

686
29:23.000 --> 29:24.930
He said he wanted to file a lawsuit,

687
29:25.680 --> 29:27.210
so I followed him to file it.

688
29:29.080 --> 29:31.640
But today in court,

689
29:34.040 --> 29:36.040
hearing the judge strike the gavel,

690
29:37.240 --> 29:38.560
I suddenly thought,

691
29:41.640 --> 29:43.280
isn't it time we woke up?

692
29:44.640 --> 29:45.640
No matter what,

693
29:47.080 --> 29:48.640
Xinxin won't come back.

694
29:49.880 --> 29:51.610
Whether we win or lose this case

695
29:53.120 --> 29:54.720
is completely meaningless.

696
29:54.800 --> 29:58.480
But getting some compensation would give us some closure.

697
29:58.880 --> 30:00.280
It's not about the money.

698
30:01.000 --> 30:02.800
It's really not about the money.

699
30:03.800 --> 30:07.240
I was the one who decided to discharge Xinxin from the hospital.

700
30:07.240 --> 30:08.480
But after she left us,

701
30:09.520 --> 30:10.880
I think every day

702
30:11.520 --> 30:13.720
about whether that decision was wrong.

703
30:14.720 --> 30:16.250
I wanted this compensation

704
30:16.520 --> 30:17.960
actually just to tell myself

705
30:17.960 --> 30:19.760
that the decision wasn't wrong.

706
30:20.880 --> 30:23.280
I don't even know who I'm fighting against.

707
30:24.360 --> 30:25.690
The insurance company,

708
30:26.440 --> 30:27.240
myself,

709
30:28.720 --> 30:30.000
or God.

710
30:31.680 --> 30:33.480
Maybe I just used the lawsuit...

711
30:34.680 --> 30:36.240
I treated it as an outlet.

712
30:38.200 --> 30:40.060
But at the other end of the outlet,

713
30:41.200 --> 30:42.730
there's actually nothing.

714
30:48.560 --> 30:49.400
Lawyer Xiao,

715
30:50.440 --> 30:51.840
thank you so much

716
30:52.120 --> 30:53.920
for always standing by our side,

717
30:54.480 --> 30:56.410
understanding and supporting us.

718
30:57.080 --> 30:57.840
Thank you.

719
31:16.440 --> 31:18.600
She must be in a really bad mood.

720
31:19.120 --> 31:21.320
We can't just watch from here.

721
31:21.560 --> 31:23.290
Going over there is even worse.

722
31:25.080 --> 31:26.610
Let her be alone for a while.

723
31:35.560 --> 31:36.480
She's up.

724
31:40.120 --> 31:41.440
Quick, Uncle, start the car.

725
31:41.440 --> 31:43.360
Wait, where is Sister Long going?

726
31:44.800 --> 31:45.960
Take your time.

727
32:12.600 --> 32:13.000
Okay.

728
32:47.040 --> 32:49.400
We have Lawyer Li to thank for this.

729
32:49.640 --> 32:52.360
The head office is very satisfied with the result.

730
32:52.360 --> 32:54.920
As expected of someone trained by you, Director.

731
32:54.920 --> 32:57.360
He already has your style from back then.

732
32:57.520 --> 32:59.480
He is much luckier than I was back then,

733
32:59.480 --> 33:01.480
having someone like you to support him.

734
33:01.480 --> 33:02.880
We support each other.

735
33:03.720 --> 33:06.400
We'll be relying on Lawyer Li more in the future.

736
33:07.120 --> 33:07.760
Mr. Chen.

737
33:08.360 --> 33:09.440
My team and I

738
33:09.440 --> 33:11.520
want to draft a new employee charter

739
33:11.720 --> 33:14.360
to help standardize the insurance company's employee training

740
33:14.360 --> 33:16.200
and prevent similar lawsuits.

741
33:16.800 --> 33:18.360
In addition, regarding insurance contracts,

742
33:18.360 --> 33:19.920
we will submit a

743
33:19.920 --> 33:21.920
targeted adjustment proposal to the industry association

744
33:21.920 --> 33:24.640
to further standardize the definition of diseases.

745
33:24.640 --> 33:25.760
This will not only prevent

746
33:25.760 --> 33:27.320
controversial cases from arising,

747
33:27.320 --> 33:29.720
but also enhance the brand's credibility.

748
33:29.840 --> 33:30.570
Sounds good.

749
33:31.240 --> 33:32.480
Come up with a proposal first,

750
33:32.480 --> 33:34.010
and I will fully support it.

751
33:34.200 --> 33:35.330
Thank you, Mr. Chen.

752
33:41.240 --> 33:42.280
You haven't left yet?

753
33:42.280 --> 33:43.010
Attorney Li,

754
33:47.200 --> 33:49.280
I'm sorry. I couldn't help it.

755
33:50.480 --> 33:51.760
I know my position.

756
33:52.600 --> 33:54.200
But I can't help but wonder

757
33:54.560 --> 33:56.680
why the law is sometimes so cold

758
33:57.160 --> 33:58.090
and so ruthless.

759
33:59.040 --> 34:00.600
Is it really fair?

760
34:06.280 --> 34:08.739
Fairness has never been a rational measure.

761
34:09.239 --> 34:11.699
Rule-making is not absolutely fair either.

762
34:13.120 --> 34:13.840
But...

763
34:13.840 --> 34:15.280
If you can't accept it,

764
34:16.480 --> 34:17.480
maybe you

765
34:19.080 --> 34:20.679
aren't cut out to be a lawyer.

766
34:24.560 --> 34:25.290
Attorney Li,

767
34:25.880 --> 34:28.080
How do you manage to always be so cold...

768
34:29.480 --> 34:30.480
so calm?

769
34:36.960 --> 34:38.639
You will meet many clients

770
34:41.000 --> 34:42.460
and encounter many cases.

771
34:43.199 --> 34:45.400
But if every client's story

772
34:46.199 --> 34:48.199
invades your emotions,

773
34:49.440 --> 34:52.300
it will not only affect your professional judgment

774
34:52.480 --> 34:54.520
but also expose you to risks.

775
34:56.520 --> 34:59.440
So establishing emotional boundaries

776
35:01.640 --> 35:04.570
is the first step to becoming a professional lawyer.

777
35:12.960 --> 35:13.720
Thank you.

778
35:14.160 --> 35:15.420
Go back and rest early.

779
36:39.760 --> 36:42.600
All right, there shouldn't be anything else today.

780
36:42.600 --> 36:43.600
Let's all go home.

781
36:45.480 --> 36:47.000
See you tomorrow, you two.

782
36:49.280 --> 36:50.040
Uncle.

783
36:50.520 --> 36:51.120
You go back first.

784
36:51.120 --> 36:53.780
I'm going to buy a couple of professional books.

785
37:35.720 --> 37:37.840
You're the director of a big law firm.

786
37:37.840 --> 37:38.960
But you drink alone.

787
37:38.960 --> 37:40.160
Why are you so stingy?

788
37:41.960 --> 37:43.000
Why are you here?

789
37:43.200 --> 37:44.400
Are you following me?

790
37:44.480 --> 37:45.920
Why would I follow you?

791
37:45.920 --> 37:47.840
Gas costs money.

792
37:47.840 --> 37:49.570
Then how did you know I was here?

793
37:49.640 --> 37:51.200
I was passing by and wanted a drink.

794
37:51.200 --> 37:52.520
And I saw you here.

795
37:54.200 --> 37:56.040
Waiter.

796
37:58.600 --> 37:59.160
Two.

797
37:59.640 --> 38:00.040
Okay.

798
38:00.040 --> 38:00.640
That's it.

799
38:01.360 --> 38:02.960
He speaks Chinese.

800
38:02.960 --> 38:04.640
Why are you speaking English to him?

801
38:04.640 --> 38:06.320
It's a bar, you have to...

802
38:06.320 --> 38:08.980
A foreign bar? Aren't you drinking Leyang beer?

803
38:09.720 --> 38:10.320
Thank you.

804
38:19.240 --> 38:20.520
I'm the one who lost the case.

805
38:20.520 --> 38:23.120
Why are you drinking like you're so depressed?

806
38:23.440 --> 38:26.080
I brought in that case.

807
38:26.440 --> 38:28.600
Losing it isn't just your problem.

808
38:30.880 --> 38:31.640
How loyal.

809
38:37.160 --> 38:39.280
You can drink, but pace yourself.

810
38:39.280 --> 38:40.640
I feel like you've already had a lot.

811
38:40.640 --> 38:43.100
If you get drunk, I won't be able to carry you.

812
38:43.800 --> 38:45.280
Are you afraid I'll drink too much?

813
38:45.280 --> 38:47.640
Then you really don't know my tolerance.

814
38:47.880 --> 38:50.840
I can drink three of you under the table.

815
38:52.320 --> 38:53.840
When I was in vocational school,

816
38:53.840 --> 38:54.640
do you know what my nickname was?

817
38:54.640 --> 38:55.360
What was it?

818
38:55.360 --> 38:57.280
A thousand cups without getting drunk.

819
38:57.280 --> 38:59.360
I even suspect I have antibodies in my body.

820
38:59.360 --> 39:00.480
What's it called?

821
39:00.480 --> 39:01.360
I just can't get drunk.

822
39:01.360 --> 39:01.920
You know?

823
39:01.920 --> 39:04.040
What's it called?

824
39:05.160 --> 39:06.000
DVD.

825
39:06.480 --> 39:08.610
What? Can you play movies in your body?

826
39:09.040 --> 39:10.520
Anyway, I have that.

827
39:10.880 --> 39:12.800
I just can't get drunk, you know?

828
39:12.800 --> 39:15.040
Alcohol antibodies, alcohol dehydrogenase, right?

829
39:15.040 --> 39:16.480
Right, what's it called?

830
39:16.480 --> 39:17.600
ADH.

831
39:17.600 --> 39:19.800
Right, see, I remembered there was a D.

832
39:20.360 --> 39:22.560
I have this. All international drinking companions have this.

833
39:22.560 --> 39:24.560
Okay, as long as you have the tolerance.

834
39:24.560 --> 39:25.320
Of course.

835
39:25.320 --> 39:25.720
Come on.

836
39:25.720 --> 39:26.320
Come on, I...

837
39:26.320 --> 39:27.040
Come on.

838
39:35.320 --> 39:36.080
Xiao Longnv.

839
39:36.520 --> 39:39.920
I've always wanted to tell you my true feelings.

840
39:40.160 --> 39:43.040
I think you're really naive.

841
39:45.400 --> 39:48.130
Are you getting bold because you had some drinks?

842
39:48.640 --> 39:49.520
Let me tell you,

843
39:50.920 --> 39:52.280
in all my life,

844
39:52.280 --> 39:54.680
I've never seen anyone do things like you.

845
39:55.080 --> 39:57.680
You really don't care about the consequences.

846
39:57.840 --> 39:59.760
Let me interview you.

847
40:00.560 --> 40:02.200
What were you thinking?

848
40:02.200 --> 40:04.460
You wanted to start a law firm on your own?

849
40:14.000 --> 40:15.480
Then let me say a few words.

850
40:18.480 --> 40:19.360
As for me,

851
40:20.320 --> 40:23.480
I just want to do what I want,

852
40:23.920 --> 40:26.480
without being tied down

853
40:26.880 --> 40:28.680
by anyone or anything.

854
40:29.800 --> 40:30.480
Right?

855
40:30.760 --> 40:32.480
It's definitely hard.

856
40:32.480 --> 40:33.880
But who doesn't have it hard?

857
40:33.880 --> 40:35.280
Just overcome it.

858
40:36.840 --> 40:37.480
As for me,

859
40:37.480 --> 40:39.920
when I first saw you setting up the stall,

860
40:39.920 --> 40:41.050
I thought to myself,

861
40:42.200 --> 40:44.160
it wouldn't last three months. It would definitely fail.

862
40:44.160 --> 40:45.640
But now,

863
40:46.280 --> 40:47.480
I really admire you.

864
40:47.760 --> 40:48.560
Do you know why?

865
40:48.560 --> 40:49.080
Why?

866
40:49.080 --> 40:50.410
Give me the microphone.

867
40:52.760 --> 40:54.220
Because there's a saying.

868
40:55.480 --> 40:56.520
I don't know if you've heard it.

869
40:56.520 --> 40:57.400
Tell me.

870
40:58.400 --> 41:00.800
God helps those who help themselves.

871
41:01.360 --> 41:03.880
Passion overcomes all difficulties.

872
41:05.400 --> 41:08.320
As long as these difficulties don't kill me,

873
41:08.480 --> 41:10.320
I'll fight to the death.

874
41:10.600 --> 41:12.130
I will definitely succeed.

875
41:14.080 --> 41:17.920
When I was at my lowest,

876
41:18.520 --> 41:20.360
you lent me a helping hand

877
41:20.720 --> 41:22.040
and brought me cases.

878
41:22.200 --> 41:23.280
I really have to thank you.

879
41:23.280 --> 41:26.200
No, you're being too polite, Along.

880
41:26.520 --> 41:27.880
As for me, I just wanted to

881
41:27.880 --> 41:29.280
make some money

882
41:29.280 --> 41:31.480
and buy a bigger house for my mom.

883
41:31.680 --> 41:32.880
You're so filial.

884
41:33.880 --> 41:35.360
My dad passed away early.

885
41:36.000 --> 41:38.840
Besides leaving me with a genetic disease

886
41:39.040 --> 41:40.160
and that bathhouse,

887
41:40.160 --> 41:41.360
he left nothing else.

888
41:41.520 --> 41:42.800
Then my mom

889
41:43.400 --> 41:45.800
raised me all by herself.

890
41:47.240 --> 41:48.400
In my memory,

891
41:48.400 --> 41:50.600
she never rested for a single day.

892
41:51.480 --> 41:54.440
I just figured I'd let her rest early

893
41:54.440 --> 41:56.000
and enjoy life.

894
41:57.320 --> 41:58.520
I couldn't tell.

895
41:58.520 --> 42:00.080
You're quite thoughtful.

896
42:00.080 --> 42:02.520
Anyway, let's not talk about this.

897
42:03.000 --> 42:04.040
I just figured,

898
42:05.040 --> 42:07.320
I don't have your

899
42:07.320 --> 42:09.040
passion or ideals.

900
42:09.840 --> 42:12.120
But when it comes to getting business,

901
42:12.880 --> 42:14.480
in this area,

902
42:16.120 --> 42:17.880
I'm the best. No problem.

903
42:18.640 --> 42:20.640
Okay, that's all I need to hear.

904
42:20.640 --> 42:23.080
We'll keep going.
